From 432cb11b41e9427d0d095fda2d09da9b7034983e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Timothy Schmidt <timschmidt@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 00:17:59 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] nvmem: qfprom: bound the MSM8926 raw read window

The maintained Fx0 fork already provides the restricted raw calibration
reader. Its keepout table ends at 4 KiB, but an oversized register window
can register a larger view and permit reads beyond the final keepout.
Reject raw windows above 4 KiB before NVMEM registration. Preserve the
existing reader, legacy programming path and mod_devicetable include.

Port the missing boundary check from the current integration feature.
This is a fork configuration-bounds issue, not a claim about a mainline
MSM8926 raw-reader vulnerability. The normal board's 4 KiB view retains
its behavior. Original author/date and copyrights remain preserved.

The LTS actual probe/read/keepout/sysfs model passes 18393 assertion
checks. The baseline fails the oversized-window assertion and reads one
synthetic word beyond the keepout. Three permission/resource/keepout
regressions are rejected under ASan, UBSan and normal LeakSanitizer.
LTS direct NVMEM callbacks return EINVAL on missing callbacks; test
expectations follow that API. No production function body is rewritten.

The QFPROM, NVMEM core and two SCM objects build on ARM normal, ARM64
normal and ARM64 RT with nonpermissive CFI, W=1 and no diagnostics.
ARM32 RT is unsupported and is not counted. Source checks do not qualify
actual fuses, firmware, voltage behavior, a full kernel link or package.

Codex prepared this local backport and qualification. Human review and
DCO remain pending; no phone operation or publication has occurred.

Backported from commit a4e91406a10be6d00011fb2e6a5b8cb3cb639751
("nvmem: qfprom: Add a restricted MSM8926 raw calibration reader")
---
 drivers/nvmem/qfprom.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/nvmem/qfprom.c b/drivers/nvmem/qfprom.c
index bce9f09dacba..cde24fa5818c 100644
--- a/drivers/nvmem/qfprom.c
+++ b/drivers/nvmem/qfprom.c
@@ -420,6 +420,10 @@ static int qfprom_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	if (IS_ERR(priv->qfpcorrected))
 		return PTR_ERR(priv->qfpcorrected);
 
+	/* Keep the raw view within the range covered by its keepout table. */
+	if (soc_data && soc_data->raw_read_only && resource_size(res) > 0x1000)
+		return dev_err_probe(dev, -EINVAL, "read-only raw view exceeds 4 KiB\n");
+
 	econfig.size = resource_size(res);
 	econfig.dev = dev;
 	econfig.priv = priv;
-- 
2.56.0

